  "name": "hotosm_mys_cultural_places",
  "notes": "Cultural and historic places from OSM. Includes museums, galleries, theatres, places of worship, monuments, and historic sites tagged via `tourism`, `amenity`, `historic`, or `heritage`. Useful for heritage protection, cultural mapping, and tourism context.\n\nOpenStreetMap is a free, collaborative world map built by volunteers. Completeness varies by region: urban areas are usually well-mapped, remote areas may be incomplete. Cross-check critical decisions with local field knowledge.\n\n- Source: [OpenStreetMap](https://www.openstreetmap.org)\n- OSM tags: [Key:tourism](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Key:tourism), [Key:amenity](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Key:amenity), [Key:historic](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Key:historic), [Key:heritage](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Key:heritage)\n- Part of many  [exports grid on HDX](https://data.humdata.org/organization/hot) by the [HOT](https://www.hotosm.org/en/)\n",
  "num_resources": 5,
  "num_tags": 3,
  "organization": {
    "id": "225b9f7d-e7cb-4156-96a6-44c9c58d31e3",
    "name": "hot",
    "title": "Humanitarian OpenStreetMap Team (HOT)",
    "type": "organization",
    "description": "**For up-to-the-minute exports from OpenStreetMap in a variety of formats for GPS and GIS, visit http://export.hotosm.org**\r\n\r\nHumanitarian OpenStreetMap Team (HOT) acts as a bridge between the traditional humanitarian responders and the OpenStreetMap Community. HOT works both remotely and physically in countries to assist the collection of geographic data, usage of that information and training others in OpenStreetMap.",
